.TH SINDOOK-INIT 1 "2026-08-31" "sindook 0.11.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
sindook-init \- create or select the default sindook identity
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sindook init
[\fB\-i\fP \fIIDENTITY\fP | \fB\-o\fP \fIFILE\fP] [\fB\-p\fP]
[\fB\-passfile\fP \fIFILE\fP] [\fB\-identity-passfile\fP \fIFILE\fP]
[\fB\-f\fP]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Creates a first identity at an explicit path, or selects an existing
one as the default identity. After init, seal, open, verify, and
rewrap use that identity automatically when no credential is given.
Sindook stores only that path and public contact aliases in its
per-user configuration; it never copies a private identity or
passphrase into the configuration directory.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-i\fP \fIIDENTITY\fP
select an existing identity as the default
.TP
\fB\-o\fP \fIFILE\fP
create a new identity here (default \fBsindook.key\fP)
.TP
\fB\-p\fP
protect a new identity with a passphrase
.TP
\fB\-passfile\fP \fIFILE\fP
read a new identity's protection passphrase from \fIFILE\fP
.TP
\fB\-identity-passfile\fP \fIFILE\fP
read an existing protected identity's passphrase from \fIFILE\fP
.TP
\fB\-f\fP
overwrite a newly-created identity
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
sindook init
sindook seal report.pdf
sindook open report.pdf.sindook
sindook init -i ~/Documents/sindook-personal.key
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sindook (1),
.BR sindook-keygen (1),
.BR sindook-paths (1)
